xilinx: route a greybox build's static side to given partition pins

-o partition-pins-route: for a net with a partition pin (-o partition-pins) and no cell
in a routing-contained pblock, route its source to the pin, or (undriven net) the pin to
each sink, outside every routing-contained pblock, before router2; lock the route.
checkRoutedDesign accepts a net whose route ends at its partition pin.

Draft, not posted. Base: router-region + pblock-replay + pblock-routethru +
partition-pins + pblock-lutff + carry-replay-order (variant partpin).

